From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:40:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 276/342] net_server: a join by address alone asks for that
 access point

The supplicant took only the network's name and chose an access point itself.
`ifconfig join <address>` went wherever that led. It now gets the address as
"bssid", which the supplicant's patch in the project reads. A join by name, and
the auto join, leave the choice to it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/net/NetServer.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/servers/net/NetServer.cpp b/src/servers/net/NetServer.cpp
index f72b649a0f..6c0daecec1 100644
--- a/src/servers/net/NetServer.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/net/NetServer.cpp
@@ -1038,10 +1038,12 @@ NetServer::_JoinNetwork(const BMessage& message, const BNetworkAddress* address,
 
 	if (name == NULL)
 		message.FindString("name", &name);
+	bool oneAccessPoint = false;
 	if (name == NULL) {
 		// No name specified, we need a network address
 		if (address->Family() != AF_LINK)
 			return B_BAD_VALUE;
+		oneAccessPoint = true;
 	}
 
 	fJoinTimes[deviceName] = system_time();
@@ -1168,6 +1170,11 @@ NetServer::_JoinNetwork(const BMessage& message, const BNetworkAddress* address,
 		status = join.AddString("name", network.name);
 	if (status == B_OK)
 		status = join.AddFlat("address", &network.address);
+	if (status == B_OK && oneAccessPoint) {
+		// joined by address alone: the supplicant is to use that one
+		status = join.AddData("bssid", B_RAW_TYPE,
+			network.address.LinkLevelAddress(), 6);
+	}
 	if (status == B_OK && !askForConfig)
 		status = join.AddUInt32("authentication", network.authentication_mode);
 	if (status == B_OK && password != NULL)
